1
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:07,880
我们死时是何种情形？
What happens when we die?

2
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:11,700
我们只是一死了之呢？
Do we simply cease to be?

3
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:16,650
还是以某种形式继续下去呢？
Or do we survive in some form?

4
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:22,780
究竟是什么造就了我们独特有意识的生物呢？
What is it that makes us unique,conscious beings?

5
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:25,240
这是最大的生存奥秘
It's the greatest mystery of existence,

6
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,680
问题看似大得连科学都难以解决
a problem seemingly too big for science to solve.

7
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:33,120
不过如今 一帮子生物学家
But today,a cluster of biologists,

8
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:34,920
物理学家 还有哲学家
physicists,and philosophers

9
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:38,790
正逼近解答这个终极问题
are closing in on the answer to the ultimate question.

10
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,510
有死后之生么？
Is there life after death?

11
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:47,040
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x01
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x01

12
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,950
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

13
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:59,580
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,620
有死后之生吗？
Is there life after death?

15
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:12,660
死亡就是终结么？
Is death the end?

16
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:14,860
是永寂么？
Eternal silence?

17
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:16,560
暗无天日么？
Blackness?

18
00:01:16,670 --> 00:01:18,460
虚无缥缈么？
Nothingness?

19
00:01:18,570 --> 00:01:22,070
抑或我们体内还有些许火花
Or is there a spark inside of us

20
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,940
生息在我们的肉体之外？
that lives on beyond our physical selves?

21
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:30,140
哲学家和科学家困扰着这个问题
Philosophers and scientists have puzzled over that question

22
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,680
已经数千年了
for thousands of years.

23
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:35,210
这是最大的谜团-
It's the great mystery --

24
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:40,280
它 迟早 我们都得面对
one that,sooner or later,we all have to face.

25
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,090
一个早晨 时年我6岁
One morning when I was 6 years old,

26
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,920
我的祖母没有醒来 -
my grandmother didn't wake up --

27
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:51,170
长眠不醒了
then or ever again.

28
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:56,600
这是我第一次感受到死亡
It was my first experience with death.

29
00:01:56,710 --> 00:02:02,370
她昨天好好的 咋今天就走了呢？
How could she be here yesterday but gone today?

30
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:04,970
她一去不返了么？
Was she gone forever?

31
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:08,660
或是去了她某些重要的生命阶段？
Or did some essential part of her live on?

32
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:16,320
基督徒和穆斯林相信好人进天堂
Christians and muslims believe in a heaven for the just

33
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:18,690
恶人下地狱
and a hell for sinners.

34
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,190
其他宗教则视死亡为变迁
Other religions see death as a transition

35
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,290
生存到一个更高的层面
to an existence on the higher plane

36
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:26,630
或地球上另一个生命
or to another life here on earth.

37
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,830
所有这些信仰都有一个共同点 -
All of these beliefs have one thing in common --

38
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:33,400
肉体只是灵魂的载体
the body is just a vessel for the soul,

39
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,980
灵魂是不灭的
and the soul is eternal.

40
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:41,310
这是许多人坚信不疑的东西
This is something many believe in their hearts,

41
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:47,650
然而有办法科学地证明或否决它么？
but is there a way to prove it or disprove it scientifically?

42
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:52,360
埃本.亚历山大执教并从事神经外科学
Eben Alexander taught and performed neurosurgery

43
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:56,330
在哈佛医学院已有15年了
at the Harvard Medical School for 15 years.

44
00:02:56,370 --> 00:03:00,270
2008年 他的职业发生了一个意想不到的转折——
In 2008,his career took an unexpected turn --

45
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:03,040
让他深刻领悟了
one that would give him profound insight

46
00:03:03,110 --> 00:03:06,600
死后之生的可能性
into the possibility of life after death.

47
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:11,110
他患上了一种罕见的细菌性脑膜炎
He contracted an extremely rare form of bacterial meningitis

48
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:14,140
陷入了深度昏迷
and fell into a deep coma.

49
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:16,610
我想如果你试图
I think if you were trying to come up

50
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:18,480
提出一个实验模型
with an experimental model

51
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:22,120
能够最接近人的死亡的话
that would best approach human death,

52
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:25,050
脑膜炎是最理想的 因为其所作所为
meningitis is perfect because what it does

53
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:28,560
就在于它攻击整个大脑的表层
is it attacks the entire outer surface of the brain.

54
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:33,730
这些是我的头颅的横断面造影
These are horizontal images taken through my skull,

55
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:37,900
你可以看到整个大脑的外层
and you can see the entire outer surface of the brain

56
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:39,740
布满了脓
was coated with pus.

57
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:42,640
这些细菌挤走了所有的葡萄糖
These bacteria had gotten rid of all the glucose,

58
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:46,540
现在患者剩下的唯一的东西就是我的脑细胞
and now the only thing left to consumer were my brain cells,

59
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,780
因此我的整个大脑皮层——
and so my entire neocortex --

60
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:49,780
就是形成我们人类的那部分大脑 -
that part of the brain that makes us human --

61
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:51,550
彻底停止运作了
was completely shut down.

62
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:54,950
弗里曼：经过7天地脑假死后
After seven days of virtual brain death,

63
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:58,860
亚历山大从昏迷中苏醒了
Alexander emerged from the coma.

64
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:02,830
出人意料 一个月里 他恢复了常态
Miraculously,within a month,he was back to normal.

65
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:06,160
但是在他离开期间他发生了一些事情
But something happened to him while he was away.

66
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:10,570
我从深度昏迷中首先回忆到的
My first recollection from deep inside the coma

67
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:13,100
是我曾经——
was that I was --

68
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:16,640
那就是我有时将其称之为蚯蚓眼世界观
it's what I sometimes call the earthworm-eye view of the world.

69
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:21,710
一切都很模糊 褐色 红色 昏暗
Everything was kind of murky,brown,red,dark.

70
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:25,220
我确实记忆挥之不去
I literally remember roots over my head.

71
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:29,190
我似乎在那里好长好长时间
And I seemed to be there for a very,very long time.

72
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,160
我没有我生前的任何记忆
I had no memory whatsoever of my life.

73
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:34,560
难以表达 开不了口
No words -- my language was gone.

74
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:36,830
我当然不知晓身边的一切
I was certainly not aware of anything going on around me

75
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,330
就在重症监护室里
in the I.C.U. room.

76
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:41,760
然后 在那过程中
And then,in the midst of that,

77
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:45,570
有一点旋律在我面前盘旋
there was a little melody that was spinning in front of me.

78
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:48,440
它开始旋转并扩大
And it just started spinning and expanded,

79
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:51,610
它最终逐渐清除了
and it ended up clearing away

80
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:56,410
整个丑陋 不祥 混沌 模糊的境界
all that ugly,foreboding,gross,muddy realm.

81
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:57,980
突然间
And all of a sudden,

82
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:03,150
我来到了一个美丽的草甸
I was coming up into this beautiful meadow.

83
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:04,850
我已没有了身体意识
I had no body awareness.

84
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:07,120
没有双臂 双腿 啥都没有
I had no arms,legs,or anything,

85
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:10,730
但我意识到我成了蝴蝶翅膀上的一个斑点——
but I was aware that I was a speck on a butterfly wing --

86
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:14,030
那是只美丽的蝴蝶
absolutely beautiful butterfly.

87
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:18,070
有无数的彩蝶
And there were millions of other colorful butterflies

88
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,140
在我们身旁飞舞
looping and swirling all around us,

89
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:22,510
组成了一支美丽的飞行大军
all in this beautiful formation of flying.

90
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:26,740
然后我们离开了这个宇宙
And then we left this Universe

91
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:30,980
进入了一个地方 我现在称其为核心
and went out into what I now call the core.

92
00:05:31,090 --> 00:05:35,590
一开始 它看上去奇大无比 暗无天日
At first,it seemed infinitely huge and dark,

93
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:38,890
尽管我来到那里时
although I was there

94
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:44,160
怀着美丽温暖的神圣意识
with that beautiful,warm awareness of the divine,

95
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:47,560
那显然是我们所谓的上帝
which was clearly what we would call God

96
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:50,430
这个地方是在宇宙之外
in this place outside the Universe.

97
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:53,940
基本上 我想起了整个多元宇宙
Basically,I recall the whole multiverse

98
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:55,440
就在我的前面
being out in front of me.

99
00:05:55,550 --> 00:05:59,040
十分清楚 爱是整个多元宇宙的
It was very clear that love was a huge part

100
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,460
举足轻重的组成部分
of the constituent of that whole multiverse.

101
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,920
弗里曼：亚历山大所面对的东西
Alexander had faced something

102
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:09,090
已有数以万计的人报告过了 -
that tens of thousands of people have reported --

103
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,120
临死的经历
a near-death experience.

104
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,860
几乎所有声称的东西
Nearly all claim something

105
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:16,030
科学至今都无法证明——
that science has so far been unable to prove --

106
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:21,100
有另一个存在于我们所了解的这个之外
that there is another existence beyond the one we know.

107
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:22,870
亚历山大博士：这个东西
This was something

108
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:28,270
很难让我从神经科学的角度给出解释
that was very difficult for me to explain from a neuroscientific standpoint,

109
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:32,980
我的科学面看不明白怎么会是这样
and the scientific side of me could not see how that could be,

110
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:34,810
然而它非常非常强大——
and yet it was a very,very powerful --

111
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,880
极强的记忆
very powerful memory.

112
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:38,980
我提出了几个模型
I came up with several models having to do

113
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,580
与神经生理学和神经解剖学有关
with the neurophysiology and neuroanatomy.

114
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:46,860
问题是那些模型中每一个能充分解释
And the problem is none of those models sufficiently explain

115
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:52,260
我从那次经历中所带回来的强烈的记忆
the very powerful memories that I brought back with me from this experience.

116
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:58,230
我最后归结到一点 我不相信
And I ended up at a point where I do not believe

117
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:03,110
神经生物学能很好地解释
that there is a good neurophysiologic explanation

118
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,640
我所发生的情况
for what happened to me.

119
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:06,640
弗里曼：埃本.亚历山大的经历
Eben Alexander's experience

120
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:10,410
是深刻而改变人生的
was profound and life-altering.

121
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:13,600
但它一点都不罕见
But it is by no means unique.

122
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:18,690
布鲁斯.格雷森是个心理医生
Bruce Greyson is a psychiatrist

123
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:21,360
供职于弗吉尼亚大学医学院
at the University of Virginia School of Medicine.

124
00:07:21,470 --> 00:07:28,770
他调查过1000多例临死经历
He has investigated more than 1,000 cases of near-death experiences.

125
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,810
临死经历的一致特征
The consistent features of near-death experiences.

126
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:36,070
是感觉到深刻的和平福祉
are a sense of profound peace and well-being,

127
00:07:36,190 --> 00:07:38,470
感觉到脱离肉体
a sense of leaving the physical body,

128
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:40,910
感觉到光亮
a sense of brilliant light

129
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:44,710
似乎焕发出温暖 无比的大爱
which seems to radiate warmth and unconditional love.

130
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:47,780
会有人报告遇到了其他人
Sometimes people report encountering other beings,

131
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,450
包括某种神祗
including a deity of some kind.

132
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:52,990
时而他们认出那神是上帝或基督
Sometimes they identify that deity as God or Christ,

133
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:54,420
时而却辨认不出
and sometimes they don't.

134
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,760
他们只是说
They just say that there was

135
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:57,690
这个全能的人物就是他们遇到的
this all-powerful being that they met.

136
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:00,760
弗里曼：许多科学家对这些经历不屑一顾
Many scientists dismiss these experiences

137
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,970
无非就是幻觉而已
as nothing more than hallucinations

138
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:06,170
是大脑在巨大的生理压力下触发的
triggered by a brain undergoing immense physical stress,

139
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:12,080
主要是神经细胞缺氧的缘故
mostly due to the nerve cells being deprived of oxygen.

140
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:14,980
早在上世纪70年代
Back in the 1970s,

141
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:17,080
美国空军的实验
experiments by the U.S. Air Force

142
00:08:17,190 --> 00:08:19,980
就无意间测试了这个概念
inadvertently tested this idea.

143
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:23,050
科学家旋转离心机里的飞行员
Scientists spun pilots in a centrifuge,

144
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:26,590
给他们的身体施加强大的重力
subjecting their bodies to massive g-forces.

145
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,890
这会造成血液从大脑流向他们的下肢
It caused blood to drain to their feet

146
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:33,400
结果他们大脑缺氧
and left their brains starved for oxygen.

147
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:35,600
他们无一例外都是暂时性失明
They invariably blacked out.

148
00:08:35,710 --> 00:08:39,700
他们醒来后 有飞行员报告说看到了亮光
When they awoke,some pilots reported seeing a bright light.

149
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,000
还有人说他们离开了自己的身体
Others said they left their bodies

150
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:44,740
在高处俯视自己——
and looked down at themselves from above --

151
00:08:44,850 --> 00:08:47,140
经历类似于
experiences similar to those of people

152
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:49,410
那些濒临过死亡的人
who have been to the brink of death,

153
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:52,580
但缺少了一个关键的特征
but lacking one key feature.

154
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,550
在他们缺氧期间
In the period when they were losing oxygen,

155
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:56,020
也是他们失去意识的过程
as they were losing consciousness,

156
00:08:56,130 --> 00:08:57,420
他们有一些特征
they had some features

157
00:08:57,530 --> 00:09:00,120
经历了某些类似于临死前的体验
which bear some similarities to near-death experiences.

158
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:03,660
不过 他们肯定没有碰到过已故的亲人
However,they certainly didn't ever meet deceased loved ones

159
00:09:03,770 --> 00:09:05,600
或其他对象
or other entities.

160
00:09:05,710 --> 00:09:10,670
所有这些生理解释带来的问题
The problem with all of these physiological explanations

161
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:15,740
在于他们并没有考虑到复杂的思想
is that they don't account for the complex thinking,

162
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:19,180
记忆的形成 感知就发生在
the memory formation,the perceptions that take place

163
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:21,040
我们知道大脑
when we know the brain

164
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:24,150
无法进行复杂的思维之时
is not capable of doing complex thinking.

165
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:26,780
弗里曼：临死经历是不是
Are near-death experiences

166
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:30,850
心中对于辞世的最后的梦想呢？
the final dream of a mind that's about to wink out of existence?

167
00:09:30,970 --> 00:09:36,330
抑或它们就是超越死亡那些东西的标志么？
Or are they a sign that there is something beyond death?

168
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:39,660
寻求真理的要求无非
Finding the truth requires nothing less

169
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:43,800
就是探索人类灵魂的科学探索
than a scientific quest to discover the human soul.

170
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:46,340
灵魂是神话呢
Is the soul a myth

171
00:09:46,450 --> 00:09:50,320
还是宇宙中的一个基本要素呢？
or one of the fundamental elements of the Universe?

172
00:09:57,910 --> 00:10:00,500
对科学家来说 死后之生的问题
For scientists,the question of life after death

173
00:10:00,610 --> 00:10:03,940
与另一个问题密切相关
is inextricably linked with another question.

174
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:06,500
意识为何物？
What is consciousness?

175
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:09,440
意识从何而来？
Where does consciousness come from?

176
00:10:09,550 --> 00:10:12,790
我们死后它将何去？
And where does it go when we die?

177
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:18,300
斯图尔特.哈梅罗夫医生是
Dr. Stuart Hameroff is the director

178
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:23,190
图森亚利桑那大学意识研究中心的主任
of consciousness studies at the University of Arizona,Tucson.

179
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:27,980
他也是一名执业麻醉师
He's also a practicing anesthesiologist.

180
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:43,150
在麻醉状态下 患者是不会做梦的 -
Under anesthesia,patients don't dream --

181
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:44,780
即使我说 做一个美梦吧
even though I said,"pick out a nice dream."

182
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,520
我们常这么说的 但没有意识了
We always say that. But there's no awareness.

183
00:10:46,630 --> 00:10:49,020
没有时间的流失 患者醒了
There's no passage of time. Patients wake up.

184
00:10:49,130 --> 00:10:51,790
他们并不知道他们究竟是睡了5分钟呢还是5个小时
They don't know if they've been asleep five minutes or five hours.

185
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,730
麻醉拿走了意识
Anesthesia takes away consciousness.

186
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,660
麻醉状态下的大脑是相当活跃的
Brain under anesthesia is quite active.

187
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:59,510
其差异还是有点神秘的
And the difference is still somewhat mysterious.

188
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:03,800
弗里曼：在手术室里多年观察病患
Years watching over patients in the operating room

189
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:07,070
让哈梅罗夫纠结于了解
made Hameroff obsessed with understanding the link

190
00:11:07,190 --> 00:11:11,340
大脑活动与意识之间的关系
between brain activity and consciousness.

191
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:13,680
当时 15年前
Then,15 years ago,

192
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:17,920
他遇到了英国大物理学家罗杰.彭罗斯爵士
he met the great British physicist,Sir Roger Penrose.

193
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:20,950
他们合作研发出了一个关于
Together,they developed a radical new theory

194
00:11:21,070 --> 00:11:22,590
大脑工作的激进新理论——
for how the brain works --

195
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:25,190
一个已经发展成了无非就是对
a theory that has grown into nothing less

196
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:29,160
灵魂不灭进行科学论证的理论
than a scientific argument for an eternal soul.

197
00:11:29,270 --> 00:11:33,270
其基础就是我们得脑细胞里的细小构造
At its root are tiny structures inside our brain cells

198
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:35,950
叫做微管
called microtubules.

199
00:11:38,350 --> 00:11:39,870
哈梅罗夫医生：你不妨看看细胞里头
If you look inside a cell,

200
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,610
你能看到这些构件
you find these structural components

201
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:45,110
宛如我们体内的骨骼
that are somewhat like the bones within our bodies.

202
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,580
微管其实发展成了丛林
The microtubules develop literally a forest

203
00:11:47,690 --> 00:11:49,110
在每个细胞内部
inside each cell,

204
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:50,850
这决定了细胞的
which determines the architecture

205
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,220
构造和结构
and the structure of the cell.

206
00:11:52,330 --> 00:11:55,790
我们认为微管设计精美
And we think microtubules are perfectly designed

207
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,760
成了细胞的机载计算机
to be the cell's onboard computer

208
00:11:57,870 --> 00:12:00,490
在分子层面上处理信息
and process information at the molecular level.

209
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:03,700
弗里曼：哈梅罗夫和彭罗斯认为微管
Hameroff and Penrose argue that microtubules

210
00:12:03,810 --> 00:12:06,500
把神经元和大脑形成整体
allow neurons and the brain as a whole

211
00:12:06,610 --> 00:12:09,330
担当了量子计算机
to function as a quantum computer,

212
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:12,140
其运作方式根本不同于
performing operations in a fundamentally different way

213
00:12:12,250 --> 00:12:15,610
普通计算机
from normal computers.

214
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:18,140
哈梅罗夫医生：这里我们看到大脑有两个半球
So,here we have a brain with two hemispheres.

215
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,510
大脑的大部分感受
Most views of the brain

216
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:22,050
是单个神经元的集合
are of a collection of individual neurons.

217
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,480
当一个神经元被激发后
When one neuron fires,

218
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,150
它就会在一个突触处发送信号给下一个神经元
it sends a signal to the next neuron at a synapse.

219
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:28,450
这样进而引发那个神经元的激发
That,in turn,causes that neuron to fire,

220
00:12:28,570 --> 00:12:30,620
那个神经元又引起另一个神经元的激发
and that neuron causes another neuron to fire,

221
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:32,120
就像多米诺骨牌一样
much like dominoes.

222
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:35,090
譬如 这里有个神经元被激发
So,for example,if a neuron fires here,

223
00:12:35,210 --> 00:12:36,630
就会触发邻居的激发
it's gonna trigger its neighbors to fire,

224
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:39,930
发送信号给整个大脑
sending signals through and around the brain.

225
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:42,510
这就是大脑工作的经典描述
That's the classical view of how the brain works.

226
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:47,440
弗里曼：在常规计算机里
In a conventional computer,

227
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:49,640
信号的传送
signals move around from place to place

228
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:53,850
是有迹可循的
along traceable paths.

229
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,520
但量子计算机的微观组件的沟通
But the microscopic components of a quantum computer

230
00:12:56,630 --> 00:13:02,520
凭借的是一个神秘的处理进程 叫做纠缠
are connected via a mysterious process called entanglement.

231
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:05,760
我们有人认为量子处理
Some of us think that quantum processes

232
00:13:05,870 --> 00:13:08,230
在大脑的意识中扮演了重要的角色
play an important role in consciousness in the brain.

233
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:11,130
举个例子 这里如果有个神经元活动
So,for example,if there's neuronal activity here,

234
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:13,730
它就有可能通过量子非局域性
it may be coupled through quantum non-locality

235
00:13:13,850 --> 00:13:15,700
耦合到这里
to processes over here.

236
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:17,970
这些神经元联系了起来
These neurons are connected

237
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,440
尽管它们相互隔开
even though they're spatially separated

238
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:21,040
这样这里的活动
so that activity here

239
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:24,240
瞬间影响到了那里的活动
instantaneously affects activity over here.

240
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:27,850
弗里曼：哈梅罗夫和彭罗斯认为
Hameroff and Penrose argue

241
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,550
一个脑细胞里的微管的变化
that a change in the microtubules in one brain cell

242
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:33,020
会影响到另一个脑细胞里的微管
can affect microbules in another.

243
00:13:33,130 --> 00:13:35,490
不过那并不尽然
But that's not all.

244
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:39,060
量子理论声称 空间中的每一个点
Quantum theory claims that every single point in space,

245
00:13:39,170 --> 00:13:43,760
即使在真空里 都能够容纳信息
even empty space,can contain information.

246
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,800
在宇宙巧夺天工的结构里
In the very fine structure of the universe,

247
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:48,570
存在有信息 量子信息
there is information,quantum information,

248
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:50,400
不会像这些多米诺骨牌这个样子
not unlike these dominoes,

249
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:54,270
我们有信息传上传下 这里那里
so that we can have information up or down,here and here,

250
00:13:54,390 --> 00:13:55,710
然而它们有了沟通
but they're connected

251
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:57,610
这样事情发生在这里
so that something that happens here

252
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,010
而影响到那里
influences something here.

253
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:03,680
弗里曼：这就意味着微管里的信息
This means the information in the microtubules

254
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,820
能够进行沟通
can connect and become entangled

255
00:14:05,930 --> 00:14:09,030
并与大脑外的宇宙纠缠在一起
with the universe outside the brain.

256
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:15,660
哈梅罗夫医生：所以 就如这两个神经元可以纠缠在一起一样
So,just like these two neurons may be entangled,

257
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:18,460
有可能意识信息
it's possible that the information of consciousness,

258
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,300
整个大脑里的 纠缠在一起
of the whole brain,is entangled

259
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:22,610
并能够逍遥存在于宇宙间
and can exist in the universe at large.

260
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,140
弗里曼：按哈梅罗夫的说法
According to Hameroff,

261
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:28,540
构建我们灵魂的是
our souls are built from something

262
00:14:28,650 --> 00:14:31,510
远比神经元更为根本的东西
much more fundamental than neurons.

263
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:35,560
它们产生于宇宙最为基本的结构
They are constructed from the very fabric of the Universe.

264
00:14:37,730 --> 00:14:40,220
哈梅罗夫医生：我认为意识或其直接前体——
I think that consciousness or its immediate precursor --

265
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:42,020
我们会称其为原意识
we'll call it proto-consciousness,

266
00:14:42,130 --> 00:14:43,820
就一直存在于宇宙间
has been in the Universe all along,

267
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:45,900
或许从大爆炸就有了
perhaps from the Big Bang.

268
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:55,930
弗里曼：所有这一切使人想起佛教和印度教的信仰
All of this recalls the Buddhist and Hindu belief

269
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:58,940
意识是宇宙不可分割的一部分
that consciousness is an integral part of the Universe,

270
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:03,720
或许充斥了整个宇宙
and perhaps it is all there is in the Universe.

271
00:15:05,890 --> 00:15:08,350
如果意识是个量子过程
If consciousness is a quantum process,

272
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:10,480
那它就可能解开一个谜团
it may solve the mystery of what happens

273
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:14,020
濒死经历期间到底发生了什么
during near-death experiences.

274
00:15:14,130 --> 00:15:16,790
哈梅罗夫医生：比方说 心脏停止跳动
Let's say the heart stops beating,

275
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:18,620
血液停止流动
the blood stops flowing,

276
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:21,090
微管失去了其量子状态
the microtubules lose their quantum state.

277
00:15:21,210 --> 00:15:25,400
但是量子信息 在微管里的
But the quantum information,which is in the microtubes,

278
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:26,970
没有被破坏
isn't destroyed.

279
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,130
它是无法破坏的
It can't be destroyed.

280
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:29,970
它只是消散到了
It just distributes and dissipates

281
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:31,340
无边的宇宙间
to the Universe at large.

282
00:15:31,450 --> 00:15:34,740
如果病患复苏 苏醒了
If the patient is resuscitated,revived,

283
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:37,710
这个量子信息就会回到微管里
this quantum information can go back into the microtubules,

284
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:40,610
于是病患就会说 我有了一次临死经历
and the patient says,"I had a near-death experience."

285
00:15:40,730 --> 00:15:42,780
我看到了白光 看到了隧道
"I saw white light. I saw a tunnel.

286
00:15:42,890 --> 00:15:44,250
我看到了死去的亲人
"I saw my dead relatives.

287
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,550
我甚至飘出了自己的肉体
I maybe even floated out of my body."

288
00:15:46,660 --> 00:15:50,220
现在 要是他们没有苏醒 患者死了
Now,if they're not revived and the patient dies,

289
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:53,190
于是就有可能这个量子信息
then it's possible that this quantum information

290
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:56,940
就可以存在于体外 或许就成了不灭的灵魂
can exist outside the body,perhaps indefinitely as a soul.

291
00:15:59,510 --> 00:16:01,700
弗里曼：许多科学家发现很难相信
Many scientists find it difficult to believe

292
00:16:01,810 --> 00:16:04,300
灵魂是量子计算机
that the soul is a quantum computer,

293
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:06,170
被连线到宇宙
hard-wired into the cosmos.

294
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:10,740
但是哈梅罗夫觉得研究正慢慢验证他的说法
But Hameroff feels that research is slowly validating his claims.

295
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:13,880
量子效应最近已经展现出
Quantum effects have recently been shown

296
00:16:13,990 --> 00:16:17,050
能控制若干重要的生物过程
to control several important biological processes,

297
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:21,120
从鸟类的导航到光合作用
from bird navigation to photosynthesis

298
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:24,120
到人类的嗅觉.
to the human sense of smell.

299
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,890
哈梅罗夫医生：迄今为止 尚无人给该理论致命打击
So far,nobody has landed a serious blow to the theory.

300
00:16:28,010 --> 00:16:31,600
我们依然行得通 证据不断——
We're still very viable,and evidence continues --

301
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,630
新的证据继续支持我们
new evidence continues to support the ideas

302
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:36,470
在15年前所提出的想法
that we put forth 15 years ago.

303
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,870
弗里曼：但是实情是
But the truth is

304
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:41,810
我们仍然不知道意识来自何处
we still don't know where consciousness comes from

305
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:44,510
我们死后它又去了何方
or where it goes when we die.

306
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:48,210
若是有办法去度量意识
If there was a way to measure consciousness,

307
00:16:48,330 --> 00:16:51,820
没准我们将能找到这些问题的答案
perhaps we could find the answers to these questions.

308
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:54,390
那个办法或许不久就将推出
That way may be coming soon,

309
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:59,060
有一位科学家在深入探索我们的思想
as one scientist explores the depths of our minds,

310
00:16:59,170 --> 00:17:02,390
希望探索确认我们身份的
hoping to discover the mysterious mental pattern

311
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:05,310
神秘的心智模式
that makes us who we are.

312
00:17:08,810 --> 00:17:11,160
人的大脑并不很大——
The human brain isn't very big --

313
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:14,830
3磅软组织
3 pounds of soft tissue.

314
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:19,810
不过它所产生的思想能够改造世界
But it can generate ideas that transform the world.

315
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,940
它能够保持多种多样的个性
It can hold personalities as diverse

316
00:17:23,060 --> 00:17:26,400
诸如马丁.路德.金和成吉思汗
as Martin Luther King and Genghis Khan.

317
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,870
它甚至都知道那是什么
It even knows what it is.

318
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:35,060
那就是自知之明 我们认为它有灵魂
It's self-aware. We think it has a soul.

319
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:38,630
但那个灵魂是从何而来的呢？
But where does that soul come from?

320
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:42,230
意识是大脑的产物么？
Is consciousness a product of the brain?

321
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:44,700
它能活得过大脑么？
And can it outlive the brain?

322
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:50,200
研究人死的时候人的大脑所发生的情况谈何容易
Studying what happens to the human brain when people die is not easy.

323
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:52,730
死亡难得见到有发信号的
Death rarely comes on cue.

324
00:17:52,850 --> 00:17:56,970
但是死亡一方面又是每天面对我们各位
But one aspect of death comes to all of us every day.

325
00:17:57,080 --> 00:18:02,590
每晚我们熟睡时 我们的意识悄然溜走了
Each night when we fall asleep,our consciousness slips away.

326
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:08,720
威斯康辛大学的朱利奥.托诺尼教授
Professor Giulio Tononi of the University of Wisconsin

327
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:11,390
正在研究我们的大脑
is studying how our brains change

328
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:13,390
在失去意识时的变化
when they lose consciousness,

329
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,390
其目的
and in doing so,

330
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:20,260
他希望揭秘究竟是什么使我们成为我们的
he's hoping to unravel the secret of what makes us us.

331
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:22,130
意识最简单明确不过了——
The simplest definition of consciousness --

332
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:25,370
就是在你熟睡无梦时 它就不见了
that which goes away when you fall into dreamless sleep.

333
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,930
然而事实上
But the fact of the matter is,

334
00:18:27,050 --> 00:18:28,840
大脑根本没有停摆
the brain doesn't shut off at all.

335
00:18:28,950 --> 00:18:32,040
神经元 神经细胞 其实活跃就如
The neurons,the nerve cells,are actually just as active,

336
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:34,940
一定程度上 如他们清醒时
in a sense,as they are when you are awake.

337
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:38,050
所以 这是个有趣的科学问题
So,it is an interesting scientific question.

338
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:40,480
那么在你不复存在时又会是怎样呢
How would it be,then,that you disappear

339
00:18:40,590 --> 00:18:42,980
而此时大脑依然还在忙碌个不停？
when your brain is still there and buzzing along?

340
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:45,790
弗里曼：托诺尼认为我们得认知水平
Tononi believes our level of awareness

341
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,890
取决于我们的大脑各部分
is determined by how much information

342
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,060
分享的信息量
the different parts of our brain share with each other.

343
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:53,560
一个丰富详尽的经验
An experience rich in detail

344
00:18:53,670 --> 00:18:56,730
将会在大脑里产生非常复杂的模式
will generate highly complex patterns in the brain,

345
00:18:56,840 --> 00:19:01,570
所产生的独特形态 托诺尼认为是可测到
creating unique shapes that Tononi believes can be measured.

346
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:05,210
每次经历基本上都好像是一个与众不同的形态
Every experience is essentially like an extraordinary shape.

347
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:09,580
就像火堆有着美丽火焰
Just like a fire with wonderful flames

348
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:12,480
其与众不同的形态每时每刻都在变幻着
is an extraordinary shape that changes all the time.

349
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:15,680
现在 给予其形态定性的东西
Now,it's a shape which is characterized

350
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,520
我将其称之为信息关系
by something I would call informational relationships.

351
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:21,560
不过其形态是内部的光照射出来的
But it's a shape that shines of inner light.

352
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:24,360
意识之火是非常特殊的火焰
The fire of consciousness is a very special fire

353
00:19:24,470 --> 00:19:26,330
它产生于大脑内部
that's generated inside the brain,

354
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,260
它需要一套非常特殊的成分
and it requires a very special set of ingredients

355
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,500
才能够燃烧并发出光芒
in order to be able to burn and shine.

356
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:34,870
弗里曼：然而要了解那火焰何时点亮
But understanding when that fire is lit

357
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:37,170
何时熄灭
and when it is extinguished

358
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:41,410
远比只是简单地读取大脑扫描来得困难
is far more difficult than simply reading a brain scan.

359
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:45,750
所以朱利奥.托诺尼构建了整个实验室
So Giulio Tononi built an entire lab

360
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:50,250
奉献给了无梦睡眠的无意识阴曹地府
dedicated to the unconscious netherworld of dreamless sleep.

361
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,720
他设计了一个实验来检测
And he designed an experiment to detect how the brain changes

362
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:55,560
我们失去意识后的大脑变化
when we lose consciousness.

363
00:19:55,670 --> 00:19:57,560
神经学这门知识相当于
It's the neurological equivalent

364
00:19:57,670 --> 00:20:00,360
叩开黑暗大宅的大门
of knocking at the door of a darkened house

365
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:02,930
来找出屋内是否有人
to find out whether anyone is home.

366
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,370
托诺尼：我们利用的东西叫做
We use something called

367
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,270
经颅磁刺激
transcranium magnetic stimulation,

368
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:11,270
这是个方法 将小电流注入大脑
which is a way to inject a little current in the brain

369
00:20:11,390 --> 00:20:13,210
无需将其打开
without having to open it up,

370
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,580
这样通过一个安全无害的方法
so in a perfectly innocuous way,

371
00:20:15,690 --> 00:20:19,750
来看看我们的大脑皮层对其的反应
and then see how our cerebral cortex reacts to it.

372
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:21,950
弗里曼：首先 研究小组在清醒状态下的
First,the team runs the experiment

373
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,150
志愿者开展实验
on a volunteer who's awake.

374
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,190
网状电极将会跟踪其
A mesh of electrodes will keep track

375
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:28,260
大脑的所有活动
of all activity in his brain.

376
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:31,990
现在 一个小磁线圈放置在他的头上
Now a small magnetic coil is placed on his head.

377
00:20:32,110 --> 00:20:35,430
启动开关 它会把持续十分之一秒钟的磁脉冲
At the flip of a switch,it delivers a pulse of magnetism

378
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:39,730
发送至他的大脑皮层
lasting a tenth of a second to his cerebral cortex.

379
00:20:39,850 --> 00:20:43,240
打击会引起小部分大脑的神经元
The burst causes neurons in a small patch of the brain

380
00:20:43,350 --> 00:20:44,740
触发
to fire,

381
00:20:44,850 --> 00:20:47,070
于是它们发出信号给其它神经元
and they,in turn,send signals to other neurons,

382
00:20:47,190 --> 00:20:50,080
同样引起它们的触发
making them fire,as well.

383
00:20:50,190 --> 00:20:52,610
这种复杂的神经活动的模式
This complex pattern of neural activity

384
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:56,080
向外扩展覆盖了约三分之一的大脑皮层
spreads out to cover about a third of the cortex

385
00:20:56,200 --> 00:21:00,920
持续了约三分之一秒钟
and lasts for almost 1/3 of a second.

386
00:21:01,030 --> 00:21:04,190
有意识的大脑反射就像是个振铃
The conscious brain reverberates like a ringing bell.

387
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:07,030
有人肯定回家了
Someone is definitely home.

388
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:10,630
然而在其无意识时又当如何呢？
But what happens when he's unconscious?

389
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:12,730
现在布雷迪睡着了
Now that Brady is asleep,

390
00:21:12,850 --> 00:21:15,200
我们要来再次振铃
we are going to ring the bell again

391
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:20,350
来看看他大脑的回应 此时 熟睡状态下
and see how his brain responds when -- after falling asleep.

392
00:21:22,390 --> 00:21:25,150
弗里曼：再一次 大脑被点亮了
Once again,the brain lights up.

393
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:29,350
但这一次 并没有反响
But this time,there is no reverberation.

394
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,920
振铃停摆
The ring of the bell dies

395
00:21:31,030 --> 00:21:33,850
就在磁脉冲关闭的那一瞬间
as quickly as the pulse of magnetism shuts off.

396
00:21:33,970 --> 00:21:36,520
沉睡的大脑可能在活动
The sleeping brain may be active,

397
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:39,290
但它已经失去了一部分大脑与另一部分之间
but it has lost the ability to share information

398
00:21:39,410 --> 00:21:42,660
分享信息的活力
between one part of the brain and another.

399
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:46,200
托诺尼认为这种信息的传播
Tononi believes this spreading of information

400
00:21:46,310 --> 00:21:49,900
是意识的关键因素
is the key ingredient of consciousness.

401
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:52,940
清醒的大脑保持专门的区域
The waking brain keeps specialized areas

402
00:21:53,050 --> 00:21:54,780
给持续的对话
in constant conversation,

403
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:56,210
就像内阁会议那样
like a Cabinet meeting

404
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:59,250
有国务卿 财政部 国防部
with the Secretary of State,Treasury,and Defense

405
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:02,620
在一起决定一个统一的行动计划
all deciding on a unified plan of action.

406
00:22:02,730 --> 00:22:05,950
大脑睡眠时 会议休会
When the brain is asleep,the meeting adjourns.

407
00:22:06,070 --> 00:22:09,990
专家不在 啥都没有作出决定
The specialists leave,and nothing gets decided.

408
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,390
为什么你入夜熟睡后会失去意识呢？
Why do you lose consciousness

409
00:22:11,510 --> 00:22:13,590
为什么你入夜熟睡后会失去意识呢？
when you are in deep sleep early in the night?

410
00:22:13,710 --> 00:22:16,230
通常在你清醒时相互交流的专家——
The specialists that normally do talk to each other

411
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:19,070
现在不这么干了
when you are awake -- they stop doing so.

412
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:22,200
你入睡后会出现某种机制
There is some mechanism that comes into place when you sleep

413
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,540
让专家之间的互动发生困难
that makes the interaction

414
00:22:23,650 --> 00:22:25,210
让专家之间的互动发生困难
between the specialists difficult.

415
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,610
结果
And,in the end,

416
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,380
看上去就好像他们再也无法相互交流了
it looks like they can't talk to each other anymore,

417
00:22:29,490 --> 00:22:31,610
毫不奇怪 所以你就失去了意识
and not surprisingly,then,you lose consciousness.

418
00:22:31,730 --> 00:22:32,950
你已不在了
You're not there anymore.

419
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:36,020
弗里曼：托诺尼分辨有意识大脑与无意识大脑
Tononi's ability to tell the difference

420
00:22:36,130 --> 00:22:38,890
之间差异的能力
between a brain that's conscious and one that's not

421
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,890
很快就有可能在医学临床上派上用场
may soon find application in a medical setting,

422
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:47,560
评估昏迷患者的意识水平
assessing the level of awareness of coma patients.

423
00:22:47,670 --> 00:22:50,060
托诺尼：你首先会关心到的是
One of the first things you would want to know is,

424
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:51,530
家里有人么？
is anybody home?

425
00:22:51,650 --> 00:22:57,040
如果某人是你的老婆 或儿子 或老妈
If that somebody is your wife or your son or your mother

426
00:22:57,150 --> 00:22:59,210
你看到眼睛张开
and you see the eyes are open

427
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:01,640
你并不知道是否有人在那里
and you don't know whether somebody's there,

428
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,250
甚至很痛苦 那你又会如何呢？
maybe even suffering,how do you go about that?

429
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:07,180
弗里曼：朱利奥.托诺尼找到了方法
Giulio Tononi has found a way

430
00:23:07,290 --> 00:23:10,150
来观察人的大脑里的意识
to see consciousness in the human brain,

431
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:14,690
但它究竟又是如何呈现在复杂的神经元网络之中的呢——
but exactly how it arises amid the complex web of neurons --

432
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:19,140
那仍是个谜 他也只能进行猜测
that remains a mystery at which he can only begin to guess.

433
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:23,430
托诺尼：若有人称意识
When one says that consciousness

434
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:27,300
需要有一个复杂的系统来支撑它
requires a complex system to support it,

435
00:23:27,410 --> 00:23:29,100
某种意义上 那必定是真的
in some sense,that must be true.

436
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:31,840
然而互联网肯定是非常复杂的
But the Internet is certainly very complex.

437
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:34,140
另一个例子 你也可以说
Another example,you could also say

438
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:37,780
下棋程序是很复杂的
that a chess-playing program is very complex.

439
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:40,610
因此有许多东西人们直观地称之为复杂
So there are many things that people intuitively call complex,

440
00:23:40,730 --> 00:23:42,080
但其中只有少数
but only a few of them

441
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:44,190
似乎能够产生意识
seem to be able to give rise to consciousness.

442
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:47,560
因此你所需要的是正确的复杂形态
So what you need is the right kind of complexity,

443
00:23:47,670 --> 00:23:51,060
只有少数结构 - 如我所知——
and only a few structures -- as far as I can tell --

444
00:23:51,170 --> 00:23:54,090
能够做到那一点 能够表现出那样非凡的技能
can do that,can pull out that extraordinary feat.

445
00:23:54,210 --> 00:23:56,260
我们的皮层 大脑皮层
Our cortex,the cerebral cortex,

446
00:23:56,380 --> 00:23:59,130
似乎近乎完美的联系在一起
seems to be wired up almost ideally

447
00:23:59,250 --> 00:24:00,980
就是为了实现那个技能的
to achieve exactly that.

448
00:24:05,550 --> 00:24:09,110
弗里曼：然而有办法揭开意识的老底么？
But is there a way to discover the root of consciousness?

449
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:11,680
自我意识感与灵魂是一回事么？
And is this sense of self-awareness

450
00:24:11,790 --> 00:24:13,680
自我意识感与灵魂是一回事么？
the same as the soul?

451
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:17,420
这个人认为他发现了人的灵魂
This man thinks he's found the human soul

452
00:24:17,530 --> 00:24:20,900
知道我们死的时候它发生了什么
and knows what happens to it when we die.

453
00:24:26,190 --> 00:24:28,610
灵魂是什么？
What is the soul?

454
00:24:29,820 --> 00:24:33,900
它是能量场么？它是实实在在的东西么？
Is it a field of energy? Is it something tangible?

455
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:35,760
它有重量么？
Does it have weight?

456
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:41,040
1907年 邓肯.麦克杜格尔博士测出
In 1907,Dr. Duncan MacDougall determined

457
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:45,920
灵魂重0.75盎司
that the soul weighs about 3/4 of an ounce,

458
00:24:46,030 --> 00:24:48,120
即21克
or 21 grams.

459
00:24:48,230 --> 00:24:53,190
他是通过称重死于结核病的患者的尸体测出的
He determined this by weighing the bodies of dying TB patients.

460
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:55,960
但是从那时起的100年里
But in the 100 years since then,

461
00:24:56,070 --> 00:24:59,660
没有人能够重复他的发现
no one has been able to replicate his findings

462
00:24:59,770 --> 00:25:05,980
因为似乎并没有什么称出来
because there doesn't seem to be anything to weigh.

463
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:14,120
会有某些难以捉摸的物质使你成为你的么？
Could there be some elusive substance that makes you you?

464
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:17,180
在存在的最小层面上
At the smallest levels of existence,

465
00:25:17,290 --> 00:25:19,400
所有的物质都是原子构成的
all matter is made of atoms.

466
00:25:19,510 --> 00:25:23,030
地球回收原子已有几十亿年了
Earth has been recycling atoms for billions of years.

467
00:25:23,370 --> 00:25:26,690
碳从树木移至海洋
Carbon moves from trees to oceans

468
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,430
移至我们身体的细胞
to the cells in our bodies.

469
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:33,730
甚至死人的原子也得到了回收利用
Even the atoms of dead people get reused.

470
00:25:33,850 --> 00:25:36,900
这意味着你股骨里的原子
This means that an atom in your thigh bone

471
00:25:37,010 --> 00:25:40,270
有可能曾经属于克利欧佩特拉(古埃及艳后)的下嘴唇
might have been part of Cleopatra's lower lip.

472
00:25:40,380 --> 00:25:45,680
这种回收并不只发生在原子层面上
And this recycling doesn't just happen at the atomic level.

473
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:51,120
你在细胞层面上不停地自我重建
You are constantly rebuilding yourself at the cellular level.

474
00:25:51,230 --> 00:25:55,850
你的身体每小时会产生10个新细胞
Your body produces 1 billion new cells every hour.

475
00:25:55,970 --> 00:25:57,560
无论你多大年纪
No matter how old you are,

476
00:25:57,670 --> 00:26:02,230
你的大部分都不会超过10岁
most of you is no more than 10 years old.

477
00:26:02,340 --> 00:26:06,300
克里斯托夫.科赫是加州理工学院的
Christof Koch is a Professor of biology and engineering

478
00:26:06,410 --> 00:26:08,100
生物和工程学教授
at Caltech.

479
00:26:08,210 --> 00:26:10,700
他认为使你成为你的
He believes that what makes you you

480
00:26:10,820 --> 00:26:14,440
完全不在于那些个原子和细胞
has nothing to do with individual atoms or cells.

481
00:26:14,550 --> 00:26:17,910
他认为你的出现之道是独一无二的
He believes that "you" emerges from the unique way

482
00:26:18,020 --> 00:26:21,380
你头脑里的细胞是有组织的
the cells in your brain are organized.

483
00:26:21,490 --> 00:26:24,120
大脑是我们所知的宇宙间最复杂的东西
The brain is the most complex piece of matter

484
00:26:24,230 --> 00:26:25,650
大脑是我们所知的宇宙间最复杂的东西
we know in the Universe.

485
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,650
人的大脑通常属于千亿神经细胞级别上的
The human brain typically is on the order

486
00:26:27,770 --> 00:26:30,050
人的大脑通常属于千亿神经细胞级别上的
of 100 billion nerve cells.

487
00:26:30,170 --> 00:26:33,560
其每一个本身就是复杂的个体
Each of those is a very complicated entity by itself.

488
00:26:33,670 --> 00:26:35,660
它宛如小电脑
It's more like a little computer,

489
00:26:35,770 --> 00:26:39,530
交互上1万至10万个其它神经细胞
interconnected to 10,000 to 100,000 other nerve cells.

490
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:43,670
弗里曼：分开来 这些神经元都是没有意识的
Separately,these neurons aren't conscious.

491
00:26:43,780 --> 00:26:46,870
但一旦它们彼此大规模交互
But when they interact with each other on a massive scale,

492
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:50,480
结果就是自我意识的网络
the result is a self-aware network.

493
00:26:50,590 --> 00:26:52,980
我们认为意识出自
We believe that consciousness emerges

494
00:26:53,090 --> 00:26:56,850
数百万乃至几十亿神经元的触发
out of the firing of millions or possibly billions of neurons.

495
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,580
那我的灵魂究竟为何物啊？
So that's what my soul is.

496
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:00,990
那是我所感受的东西 我的主观感受
That's what my feelings,my subjective feelings

497
00:27:01,100 --> 00:27:03,120
痛苦啊 快乐啊 向往啊
of pain and pleasure and of yearning are.

498
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:05,560
弗里曼：但要是 正如科赫所认为的
But if,as Koch believes,

499
00:27:05,670 --> 00:27:08,660
我们的脑干若完全就是这个脆弱
who we are stems exclusively from this fragile

500
00:27:08,770 --> 00:27:11,060
千变万化的脑细胞网络构成的话
and ever-changing network of brain cells,

501
00:27:11,180 --> 00:27:13,730
那么就不会有永恒的你
then there can be no eternal you.

502
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:15,130
科赫：我们不断地变化
We constantly change.

503
00:27:15,250 --> 00:27:17,240
对于每一个经历 我们都有所变化
With each experience,we change a little bit.

504
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:19,100
对于某些经历 我们变化较多
With some experiences,we change more,

505
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:21,270
而对于其他经历 我们则变化较少
and with other experiences,we change less.

506
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:23,580
所以从那个意义上 并无定数
So,that sense,there's no constant.

507
00:27:23,690 --> 00:27:26,680
随着我们年龄增长的有 我的思想 我的身体
And as we age,again,my mind -- my body,

508
00:27:26,790 --> 00:27:29,250
同时还有我的个性 我思想的变化
but also my personality and my mind changes.

509
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:32,820
所以从那个意义上 并没有永恒不变的个性
So,that sense,there's no constant personality.

510
00:27:32,930 --> 00:27:36,750
这是大脑结构的不断变化 也是大脑推动的不断变化
It's a changing construct of the brain and by the brain.

511
00:27:36,870 --> 00:27:41,290
弗里曼：这种大脑观称之为唯物主义
This view of the brain is called materialism,

512
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:43,560
科赫是其倡导者
and Koch is its champion.

513
00:27:43,670 --> 00:27:45,000
对于唯物主义者来说
For materialists,

514
00:27:45,110 --> 00:27:47,800
灵魂只不过是一个稍纵即逝的幻觉
the soul is nothing more than a fleeting illusion,

515
00:27:47,910 --> 00:27:50,500
幻觉长不过产生其的物理网络
an illusion that cannot outlive

516
00:27:50,620 --> 00:27:53,050
幻觉长不过产生其的物理网络
the physical network from which it arises.

517
00:27:56,090 --> 00:27:58,780
一旦电流沟通中止
Once that electrical traffic ceases

518
00:27:58,890 --> 00:28:00,810
缘于大脑本身已不再工作
because the brain itself doesn't work anymore

519
00:28:00,930 --> 00:28:02,850
神经元停止触发
and the neurons stop firing,

520
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:06,960
那么灵魂也将不复存在
then,also,the soul will cease to exist.

521
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:12,620
弗里曼：但知名认知科学家道格拉斯.霍夫斯塔德
But renowned cognitive scientist Douglas Hofstadter

522
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:16,230
并不那么快地否认死后之生的可能性
is not so quick to dismiss the possibility of life after death.

523
00:28:16,340 --> 00:28:19,860
他认为灵魂并非我们一咽气就消失的
He believes the soul does not disappear the moment we die.

524
00:28:19,980 --> 00:28:22,400
霍夫斯塔德：在我还是物理学研究生时
When I was a graduate student in physics,

525
00:28:22,510 --> 00:28:26,140
我有一个我很喜欢的教授
I had a professor who I was very fond of

526
00:28:26,250 --> 00:28:31,140
他是个宗教人士
who was a religious person.

527
00:28:31,260 --> 00:28:37,080
他相信 让我很震惊 惊讶 困惑
And he believed,to my shock and surprise and confusion,

528
00:28:37,190 --> 00:28:39,580
在大脑里面
that inside the brain,

529
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:42,150
存在有某种粒子
there were certain kinds of particles

530
00:28:42,270 --> 00:28:44,620
是我们尚未发现的
that we hadn't yet discovered

531
00:28:44,740 --> 00:28:48,030
带来了灵魂和意识
that gave rise to soul and consciousness.

532
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:50,330
弗里曼：霍夫斯塔德对大脑采取了
Hofstadter took a more scientific approach

533
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:51,730
更科学的手段
to the brain.

534
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:55,330
他已是模拟复杂心理过程的先驱
He became a pioneer in modeling complex mental processes.

535
00:28:55,450 --> 00:28:58,340
他思考人们的思考
He thinks about how people think.

536
00:28:58,450 --> 00:29:01,640
人类做得最好的 在他看来
And what humans do best,in his opinion,

537
00:29:01,750 --> 00:29:05,180
就是制作了周围世界的心智地图
is make mental maps of the world around them.

538
00:29:05,290 --> 00:29:08,310
感知世界的过程
The process of perceiving a world

539
00:29:08,430 --> 00:29:12,280
产生了万物的内部表示
gives rise to internal representations of everything.

540
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:14,820
你知道 如果我看到这个胡椒瓶
You know,if I look at this pepper shaker,

541
00:29:14,930 --> 00:29:17,990
我就有了它的内在模型
I have an internal model of it.

542
00:29:18,100 --> 00:29:19,660
我无需去观察它
And I don't need to look at it

543
00:29:19,770 --> 00:29:21,730
因为我已见到它好多回了
because I've seen it so many times,

544
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:24,360
我已经有了它固定的内在模型了
I have an internal model of it that is stable.

545
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:28,030
弗里曼：所有的动物都会制作心智地图
All animals make mental maps.

546
00:29:28,150 --> 00:29:31,700
动物越大 地图就越复杂
The bigger the animal,the more complex the map.

547
00:29:31,820 --> 00:29:35,610
蜜蜂知道太阳和它的蜂巢的方位
A bee knows the position of the sun and its hive.

548
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:37,540
蝠鲼学习遨游在
A manta ray learns to navigate

549
00:29:37,660 --> 00:29:42,050
错综复杂的洋流里
the convoluted web of ocean currents.

550
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,620
狒狒必须遵循
A baboon must keep track

551
00:29:43,730 --> 00:29:47,320
大队人马尊卑有序的社会秩序
of the troop's social pecking order.

552
00:29:47,430 --> 00:29:48,750
我们地图的构建
Our maps are built

553
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:51,820
来自我们所遇到的人和物的寿命…
from a lifetime of objects and people we've encountered...

554
00:29:51,940 --> 00:29:54,590
还有另外一个关键因素
And one other crucial element.

555
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:59,230
霍夫斯塔德：我们不仅吸纳了其余的世界
We incorporate not only the rest of the world,

556
00:29:59,340 --> 00:30:01,670
我们还吸纳了我们对我们是谁
but we incorporate our own understanding

557
00:30:01,780 --> 00:30:04,000
我们是什么的自我认识
of who we are and what we are,

558
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:08,210
这里包括了肤浅 有形的东西
which includes superficial,physical things

559
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:10,110
比如事实上我们有两只手
like the fact that we have two hands

560
00:30:10,220 --> 00:30:12,410
每只手有五个指头
and five fingers on each hand,

561
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:15,080
我们所具有的那种幽默感
what kind of sense of humor we have,

562
00:30:15,190 --> 00:30:18,280
我们是否擅长于篮球的远距离投篮
whether we're good at throwing free-throws in basketball

563
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,880
或是勾手投篮
or hook shots.

564
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:25,990
我们创造了一个概念 反映了我们是谁
And we create a concept that reflects who we are.

565
00:30:26,100 --> 00:30:29,630
弗里曼：霍夫斯塔德把这个世界地图
Hofstadter regards this map of the world

566
00:30:29,740 --> 00:30:32,200
同时也包括了地图制作者的地图
that also includes a map of the map-maker

567
00:30:32,310 --> 00:30:34,610
看作是心智反馈回路
as a mental feedback loop.

568
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:39,400
如果你将摄像机对准电视机屏幕
If you point a television camera at a television screen

569
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:42,240
于是屏幕就摄入了自己
and then the screen gets put onto itself,

570
00:30:42,350 --> 00:30:43,710
等等 等等
et cetera,et cetera,

571
00:30:43,820 --> 00:30:46,540
你看到了一个非常复杂的视觉模式 -
and you get a very complex visual pattern --

572
00:30:46,660 --> 00:30:49,510
系统本身就是自我感知
the system itself is perceiving itself.

573
00:30:49,630 --> 00:30:52,780
对我来说 灵魂是个浮现过程
To me,the soul is an emergent process,

574
00:30:52,900 --> 00:30:55,190
一个几十年感知和反馈所产生的浮现体
an emergent entity that comes out of decades

575
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:59,760
一个几十年感知和反馈所产生的浮现体
of perception and feedback.

576
00:30:59,870 --> 00:31:02,560
弗里曼：但这个意识观
But this view of consciousness

577
00:31:02,670 --> 00:31:04,530
具有震撼的影响
has a shocking implication.

578
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:08,270
若说灵魂只是个奇怪的心智反馈回路
If the soul is just a strange mental feedback loop,

579
00:31:08,380 --> 00:31:11,240
那么它不该是人类独有的
then it should not be unique to humans.

580
00:31:11,350 --> 00:31:15,810
任何足够聪明的网络都应该能够体验它
Any sufficiently smart network should be able to experience it,

581
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:18,040
不管它是何物
whatever it is made of.

582
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:20,510
这就是为什么这个当代科学怪人
Which is why this latter-day Frankenstein

583
00:31:20,620 --> 00:31:23,210
正在计划打造一个灵魂
is planning to build a soul.

584
00:31:23,330 --> 00:31:27,100
他所研究的能够直指死后之生
What he learns could point the way to a life beyond death.

585
00:31:29,570 --> 00:31:33,570
宗教告诉我们我们的灵魂能够超脱凡体
Religion tells us that our souls transcend the body.

586
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:40,820
这些只是我们世上走一回的皮囊而已
These are just shells that we walk a around in for a while.

587
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:44,160
大多数科学家并不以为然
Most scientists don't believe that.

588
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:47,300
他们称我们所谓的灵魂
They say that what we call the soul

589
00:31:47,410 --> 00:31:50,100
是大脑构成的自我意识的网络
is a self-aware network of brain connections

590
00:31:50,210 --> 00:31:53,470
已经进化了数百万年了
that evolved over millions of years.

591
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:56,070
如果那时真的
If that's true,

592
00:31:56,190 --> 00:32:01,010
那么如果我们来打造一个人脑的拷贝又当如何呢？
then what would happen if we built a copy of the human brain?

593
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:03,240
它会有灵魂么？
Would it have a soul?

594
00:32:03,550 --> 00:32:06,370
我们即将有所突破
We're on the verge of finding out.

595
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:08,270
如果思想之谜
And if the mystery of the mind

596
00:32:08,380 --> 00:32:11,040
是我们能够破解的东西
is something we can crack computationally,

597
00:32:11,150 --> 00:32:16,720
那么它甚至可以给我们死里逃生的路线
it would even give us an escape route from death.

598
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:23,220
世界各地的研究人员
Around the world,teams of researchers

599
00:32:23,330 --> 00:32:27,820
正在尝试逆向构建人脑
are attempting to reverse-engineer a human brain.

600
00:32:27,940 --> 00:32:31,530
这是个艰巨的任务 因为对于我们所有的研究来说
It's a tough job,because for all our research,

601
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:34,400
大脑仍然是已知的宇宙间
the brain is still the most complicated instrument

602
00:32:34,510 --> 00:32:37,100
最为复杂的仪器
in the known Universe.

603
00:32:37,210 --> 00:32:40,300
然而绘制大脑可能需要几十年时间才能完成
But mapping the brain could take decades to complete,

604
00:32:40,420 --> 00:32:42,170
这就是为什么有些离经叛道的科学家
which is why some rebel scientists

605
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:44,070
决定利用鲜活的脑细胞
have decided to harness the firepower

606
00:32:44,190 --> 00:32:47,780
内部的火力
inside living brain cells.

607
00:32:47,890 --> 00:32:50,050
他们试图破解灵魂之谜
They're trying to crack the secrets of the soul

608
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:54,220
通过将生物学和技术融合在一起
by fusing biology and technology,

609
00:32:54,330 --> 00:32:59,020
去上一些大脑并将它们杂交到一些硬件上
taking bits of brain and mating them to bits of hardware.

610
00:32:59,130 --> 00:33:01,360
大多数计算机模拟
Most computer simulations

611
00:33:01,470 --> 00:33:05,730
被限制在非常单纯的神经元上
are limited to very simplistic neurons.

612
00:33:05,840 --> 00:33:08,130
我们这里培养皿里的东西
What we have here in our culture dishes

613
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:11,230
用得是鲜活的神经元
with real,live,wet,squishy neurons

614
00:33:11,350 --> 00:33:12,800
完全利用它们的复杂性
with all their complexity,

615
00:33:12,920 --> 00:33:15,270
其大大复杂于我们在
is immensely much more complicated

616
00:33:15,380 --> 00:33:17,540
今天的计算机上所做的任何模拟
than anything we can simulate on today's computers.

617
00:33:17,650 --> 00:33:20,480
弗里曼：史蒂夫.波特教授
Professor Steve Potter

618
00:33:20,590 --> 00:33:22,910
任职于乔治亚技术学院
of the Georgia Institute of Technology

619
00:33:23,030 --> 00:33:25,380
设计打造的大脑 -
designs and builds brains --

620
00:33:25,490 --> 00:33:28,580
半生命半机器大脑
brains that are half-living,half-machine.

621
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:33,420
波特的研究小组从大鼠胚胎中提取培养的神经元
Potter's team takes neurons cultured from rat embryos

622
00:33:33,540 --> 00:33:36,790
然后将它们种植在微型电极板上
then grows them on miniature plates of electrodes.

623
00:33:36,910 --> 00:33:39,730
波特：这是个多电极阵列培养皿
Here is a multi-electrode array culture dish.

624
00:33:39,840 --> 00:33:43,430
你可以看到荧光示踪神经元生长在上面
You can see some fluorescently labeled neurons growing on it.

625
00:33:43,550 --> 00:33:45,330
这些是电极
These are the electrodes

626
00:33:45,450 --> 00:33:48,600
通过导线拦截电子
with leads heading off to the electronics

627
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:52,380
那是我们用来记录和刺激那些细胞的电子
that we use to record from and stimulate the cells.

628
00:33:52,490 --> 00:33:54,740
这些全都是轴突和树突
These are all the axons and dendrites

629
00:33:54,860 --> 00:33:57,750
表示细胞之间的联系
that represent the connections between the cells.

630
00:33:57,860 --> 00:34:00,750
这些联系形成于
Those connections form

631
00:34:00,860 --> 00:34:03,420
头四个小时的培养过程中
over the course of the first four hours in culture.

632
00:34:03,530 --> 00:34:05,920
你这里可以看到时间推移
You can see on this time lapse here

633
00:34:06,030 --> 00:34:07,790
联系的形成过程
connections forming.

634
00:34:07,900 --> 00:34:10,290
这些就是突触连接
So,those are the synaptic connections

635
00:34:10,410 --> 00:34:12,430
这样神经元就可以彼此交流
by which the neurons talk to each other,

636
00:34:12,540 --> 00:34:15,930
我们可以拍摄到过程中的对话
and we can film that conversation in progress

637
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:18,630
利用这里的钙敏感染色剂
using a calcium-sensitive dye here.

638
00:34:18,750 --> 00:34:21,000
这样你就可以看到细胞不停闪烁
So,here you can see the cells flashing.

639
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:23,210
每当有细胞发送信号给另一个细胞时
Every time the cell sends a signal to another cell,

640
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:24,770
都会有一个爆裂的钙
it has a little burst of calcium.

641
00:34:24,890 --> 00:34:27,810
弗里曼：大脑长成后
When the brain has grown,

642
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:31,510
波特会通过电极给它发送信息
Potter send information to it through the electrodes,

643
00:34:31,630 --> 00:34:34,350
大脑会做出反应
and the brain responds.

644
00:34:34,460 --> 00:34:36,920
那些电极接到计算机上
Those electrodes are connected to a computer

645
00:34:37,030 --> 00:34:40,760
计算机连上一架机器人
that's wired up to a robot body,

646
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:43,630
结果形成了新的生命
resulting in a new form of life.

647
00:34:43,740 --> 00:34:46,300
这是hybrot（杂种机器人）-
This is hybrot --

648
00:34:46,410 --> 00:34:50,000
由活脑组织控制的机器人
a robot controlled by living brain tissue.

649
00:34:50,110 --> 00:34:51,800
其大脑在冰柜里
Its brains are in a refrigerator,

650
00:34:51,910 --> 00:34:55,770
不过你在计算机屏幕上能看到其神经元的反应
but you can see its neurons react on the computer screen

651
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:59,510
同时其身体在实验台上寻找出路
as its body finds its way around the lab bench.

652
00:34:59,620 --> 00:35:01,480
和任何动物一样
Like any animal,

653
00:35:01,590 --> 00:35:04,150
hybrot在从中体验和学习
the hybrot has experiences and learns from them.

654
00:35:04,260 --> 00:35:07,950
在这里 是如何定位其环境的呢
In this case,how to navigate its environment.

655
00:35:08,060 --> 00:35:13,500
那么问题在于hybrot能够有意识么？
So,the question is,could a hybrot ever become conscious?

656
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:20,260
我们能否得到培养成联网的意识
Whether or not we could ever get to conscious cultured networks

657
00:35:20,380 --> 00:35:23,970
这个问题 要我说 我们已经有个答案 - 可以
is a question which I would say we've already answered "yes."

658
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,500
我们看到培养皿
We have culture dishes

659
00:35:25,610 --> 00:35:27,500
不断接收到环境输入的信息
that are receiving inputs from the environment.

660
00:35:27,620 --> 00:35:29,510
它们以复杂的方式来应对它们
They're responding to them in complicated ways.

661
00:35:29,620 --> 00:35:32,310
所以它们有自己的环境意识
So they're conscious of their environment

662
00:35:32,420 --> 00:35:33,980
某些非常初步的方式
in some very rudimentary fashion.

663
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:36,180
或许对于较为复杂的互动
Perhaps with more complicated interactions

664
00:35:36,290 --> 00:35:37,710
存在于不同脑组织之间的
between different brain tissues

665
00:35:37,830 --> 00:35:39,720
以及计算机与脑组织之间的
and between the computer and the brain tissues,

666
00:35:39,830 --> 00:35:42,120
我们所得到的东西 人们会说
we could get to something that people would say

667
00:35:42,230 --> 00:35:45,960
是高水平的认知 更像是人的意识
is a high-level cognition,more like human consciousness.

668
00:35:46,070 --> 00:35:50,160
弗里曼：但要是有朝一日 hybrot或计算机被唤醒
But if one day a hybrot or a computer wakes up

669
00:35:50,270 --> 00:35:53,060
意识到它是什么 它是谁
and realizes what and who it is,

670
00:35:53,180 --> 00:35:55,930
要是有灵魂从那些导线里冒出来
if a soul emerges from those wires,

671
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:58,670
我们如何知道呢？
how would we know?

672
00:35:58,780 --> 00:36:02,140
我们得全靠对话了
We'll have to rely on conversation.

673
00:36:02,250 --> 00:36:05,140
我们不妨询问人造大脑 你有意识么？
If we asked the artificial brain,"are you conscious?"

674
00:36:05,250 --> 00:36:07,240
它说服我们说它有
And it persuades us that it is,

675
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:09,380
那我们就只好采信它了
we'll just have to take its word.

676
00:36:09,490 --> 00:36:12,210
不过同样的事情在我们与别人交流时也会碰到
But the same thing applies when we talk to other humans.

677
00:36:12,330 --> 00:36:15,420
我们其实并不知道别人是否有意识
We don't actually know that other people are conscious.

678
00:36:15,530 --> 00:36:19,160
他们没准只是行尸走肉而已 说着人话
They might just be zombies who are saying the right thing

679
00:36:19,270 --> 00:36:22,170
但却没有亲身 主观的经历
but having no private,subjective experience.

680
00:36:24,340 --> 00:36:28,030
我现在就可以将某些人工智能
I can put some sort of an artificial intelligence

681
00:36:28,140 --> 00:36:29,430
放到计算机里去
into a computer right now

682
00:36:29,550 --> 00:36:31,730
代表我可能会做出的某种决定
that represents the kind of decisions I might make

683
00:36:31,850 --> 00:36:35,440
某种意义上 它具有了我的某种意识
and has,in some sense,some of my consciousness in it.

684
00:36:35,550 --> 00:36:37,240
所以那是不难做到的
So that's not hard to do.

685
00:36:37,350 --> 00:36:38,910
但是要得到的东西是我们所说的
But to get something that we would say

686
00:36:39,020 --> 00:36:40,680
是我的意识足够好的副本
is a good enough copy of my consciousness

687
00:36:40,790 --> 00:36:43,410
并且若是将它放入别人的体内
that if it were put back in somebody else's body,

688
00:36:43,530 --> 00:36:46,080
人们就会误认为它就是我——
people would be fooled into thinking it was me --

689
00:36:46,190 --> 00:36:48,780
这种事情我们甚至还没有头绪
this is something we haven't even the first clue

690
00:36:48,900 --> 00:36:51,420
究竟如何以一种详细的方法去做到
of how to do it in any kind of a detailed way.

691
00:36:51,530 --> 00:36:55,590
弗里曼：打造我们灵魂的人造家园
Building artificial homes for our souls

692
00:36:55,700 --> 00:36:58,160
或许还要等上好长时间
may be a long time coming,

693
00:36:58,270 --> 00:37:01,000
那么在此期间我们要做些什么呢？
so what do we do in the meantime?

694
00:37:01,110 --> 00:37:02,970
原来搭载我们身后灵魂的理想载体
Turns out the ideal vessels

695
00:37:03,080 --> 00:37:06,070
原来搭载我们身后灵魂的理想载体
to carry souls after the death of the body

696
00:37:06,180 --> 00:37:08,670
可能已经存在
may already exist.

697
00:37:08,780 --> 00:37:12,450
有可能就在你的身旁
One could be sitting right next to you.

698
00:37:16,010 --> 00:37:18,200
尽管我们有先进的技术
Despite our advanced technology,

699
00:37:18,970 --> 00:37:23,830
但生命之谜的破解看似依然遥遥无期——
the riddle of life still seems a long way from being solved --

700
00:37:24,090 --> 00:37:27,790
这个…是这回事么？
or...Is it?

701
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:30,720
印第安纳州布卢明顿
In Bloomington,Indiana,

702
00:37:30,830 --> 00:37:35,790
道格拉斯.霍夫斯塔德称这全在于视角
Douglas Hofstadter says it's all a matter of perspective.

703
00:37:35,910 --> 00:37:39,330
他认为意识是大脑以奇妙的方式汇集信息
He believes consciousness is the inevitable result

704
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:41,130
他认为意识是大脑以奇妙的方式汇集信息
of the strange and wonderful way

705
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:43,530
形成思维模式的必然结果
the brain joins information together

706
00:37:43,650 --> 00:37:45,900
形成思维模式的必然结果
into patterns of thought.

707
00:37:46,020 --> 00:37:48,940
形成我们的思维模式
And the patterns of thought that form us

708
00:37:49,050 --> 00:37:51,880
并非我们的独享
are not unique to us.

709
00:37:51,990 --> 00:37:54,780
我们全都好奇地拼凑着
We are all curious collages

710
00:37:54,890 --> 00:37:57,920
我们打过交道的旁人
of everyone we've ever been influenced by,

711
00:37:58,030 --> 00:38:00,450
不管是生是死
living or dead.

712
00:38:00,560 --> 00:38:02,050
你灵魂的模式
The pattern of your soul

713
00:38:02,170 --> 00:38:05,290
是你自己头脑里最强最复杂的
is the strongest and most complex in your own brain,

714
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:08,440
但它能够传递给其它大脑
but it can be passed on to other brains.

715
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:13,840
霍夫斯塔德：这是肖邦的练习曲
This is a book of Chopin Atudes.

716
00:38:14,110 --> 00:38:18,200
这些白纸黑符
These black splotches on white paper

717
00:38:18,320 --> 00:38:22,240
捕捉到了肖邦情感中
capture some very,very central pieces

718
00:38:22,350 --> 00:38:23,970
最核心的部分——
of Chopin's emotionality --

719
00:38:24,090 --> 00:38:28,550
他的高潮 他的低潮
his highs,his lows,

720
00:38:28,660 --> 00:38:30,050
他的成就感
his sense of triumph,

721
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:34,020
他的挫折感 痛苦感
his sense of resignation or anguish.

722
00:38:34,130 --> 00:38:37,720
凡此种种就是流露出来的他的情感构成
Anything that was part of his emotional makeup comes through,

723
00:38:37,830 --> 00:38:40,620
让别的人类深入洞察的东西
and one gets a very deep glimpse of another human being.

724
00:38:40,740 --> 00:38:43,730
或许在此人正式从地球表面消失150、160年后
Perhaps 150,160 years after that person

725
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:47,730
或许在此人正式从地球表面消失150、160年后
has officially vanished from the surface of the earth,

726
00:38:47,840 --> 00:38:49,830
他们的一些灵魂依然存在
something of their soul persists

727
00:38:49,950 --> 00:38:54,670
侵袭着无数其他人的思想和大脑
and invades the minds and brains of millions of other people.

728
00:38:54,790 --> 00:38:58,510
弗里曼：这是一种死后的生命形式
This is a form of life after death

729
00:38:58,620 --> 00:39:00,480
我们都要经历的
that we all experience,

730
00:39:00,590 --> 00:39:03,590
尽管我们可能无法识别它是什么
though we may not recognize it for what it is.

731
00:39:05,660 --> 00:39:09,220
弗里曼：就是一个巨大的个人悲剧 让霍夫斯塔德看到这个的——
It took a great personal tragedy for Hofstadter to see this --

732
00:39:09,330 --> 00:39:12,030
他太太卡罗尔的去世
the death of his wife,Carol.

733
00:39:14,500 --> 00:39:15,930
我们过去生活在意大利
We were in Italy,

734
00:39:16,040 --> 00:39:20,200
很突然发现了脑肿瘤
and it was a very sudden discovery of a brain tumor.

735
00:39:20,310 --> 00:39:23,500
我们发现她患上了脑肿瘤时
And we only found out that she had a brain tumor

736
00:39:23,610 --> 00:39:26,270
是在12月11日
on the 11th of December,

737
00:39:26,380 --> 00:39:28,110
到12月12日 晚间
and on the 12th of December,in the evening,

738
00:39:28,220 --> 00:39:30,470
她陷入了昏迷
she fell into a coma.

739
00:39:30,590 --> 00:39:35,810
一切非常非常块
So it was very,very,very fast.

740
00:39:35,930 --> 00:39:38,350
当时我一直以来打交道
When somebody that I have been entangled with

741
00:39:38,460 --> 00:39:40,250
如此长如此深的人
for so long and so deeply

742
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:42,720
突然之间撒手人寰
is suddenly poofed out of existence,

743
00:39:42,830 --> 00:39:46,760
于是我不得不 你知道 面对的问题就是
I then had to,you know,confront the question

744
00:39:46,870 --> 00:39:50,160
究竟有无幸存下来的东西
of what,if anything,survived

745
00:39:50,270 --> 00:39:52,100
以及在哪里 总之
and where,if at all,

746
00:39:52,210 --> 00:39:56,530
人的灵魂能够移植
can a human soul be transplanted,

747
00:39:56,650 --> 00:39:59,500
从一个大脑移至另一个大脑么？
uprooted from one brain to another brain?

748
00:39:59,620 --> 00:40:04,480
我的答案就必须是
And my answer would have to be,

749
00:40:04,590 --> 00:40:08,080
在一个极其有限的意义上说 可以
in a very limited sense,yes.

750
00:40:08,190 --> 00:40:11,920
就卡罗尔存在于我内心而言——
The degree to which Carol exists inside me --

751
00:40:12,030 --> 00:40:16,250
那是个简装版的她
it's a much stripped-down version of her.

752
00:40:16,370 --> 00:40:19,920
那是简陋版 粗糙的
It's a crude version. It's coarse-grained.

753
00:40:20,040 --> 00:40:22,360
仿佛就是一件镶嵌作品
It's as if one had a mosaic done

754
00:40:22,470 --> 00:40:27,060
用了很小很小的精美石子——
in very,very small,fine stones --

755
00:40:27,180 --> 00:40:28,570
上百万颗
a million of them.

756
00:40:28,680 --> 00:40:30,800
然后它被毁了
And then it was a destroyed,

757
00:40:30,910 --> 00:40:32,800
但是有人 在其被毁之前
but somebody,before it was destroyed,

758
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:36,670
已经复制了它 只是用了1000块石头
had made a copy of it but only using 1,000 stones.

759
00:40:36,790 --> 00:40:38,940
因此这1000块石头
And so the 1,000 stones

760
00:40:39,060 --> 00:40:41,580
仍然具有同样的颜色 同样的布置
still have the same colors and the same kind of arrangement,

761
00:40:41,690 --> 00:40:44,550
但要粗糙很多 不同的介质
but much more coarse-grained,in a different medium,

762
00:40:44,660 --> 00:40:46,220
不同的石头
in different stones.

763
00:40:46,330 --> 00:40:47,950
原版的已经毁了
The original has been destroyed,

764
00:40:48,060 --> 00:40:53,260
但副本以粗糙的版本幸存了下来
but the copy exists in a coarse-grained version.

765
00:40:53,370 --> 00:40:56,360
弗里曼：因而 我们还在
And so,we live on.

766
00:40:56,470 --> 00:40:58,830
我们灵魂的片段存活在
A piece of our soul survives

767
00:40:58,940 --> 00:41:01,400
我们曾经接触过的每一个人心里
in everyone we have ever encountered.

768
00:41:01,510 --> 00:41:03,000
那个灵魂碎片
That soul fragment

769
00:41:03,110 --> 00:41:06,470
最强烈 最被认可
is the strongest,most recognizable

770
00:41:06,580 --> 00:41:08,410
存在于爱我们的人心里
in the people who loved us.

771
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:12,440
这种死后之生是我们都能涉及到的
This form of life after death is one we can all relate to,

772
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:14,410
无论我们信仰什么
whatever our religion.

773
00:41:14,520 --> 00:41:18,380
但有木有灵魂别的安身之地呢？
But is there some other resting place for the soul?

774
00:41:18,500 --> 00:41:21,290
我们在地球上最后时刻
Does our consciousness just shimmer out of existence

775
00:41:21,400 --> 00:41:23,720
我们的意识就只是灵光一现么？
in our last moments on earth?

776
00:41:23,830 --> 00:41:27,160
灵魂是不是无非就是神经处理网络
Is the soul nothing more than a network of neural processes,

777
00:41:27,270 --> 00:41:30,560
是能够有朝一日在机器里再现的呢？
something that one day can be recreated in a machine?

778
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:33,260
抑或我们大脑里的量子状态
Or does the quantum state of our brain

779
00:41:33,380 --> 00:41:36,900
是不是全部重新吸入宇宙呢？
get reabsorbed into the Universe at large?

780
00:41:37,010 --> 00:41:40,000
科学家认为他们最终在接近
Scientists believe they are finally getting close

781
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:42,170
解决这个谜团
to solving this puzzle,

782
00:41:42,290 --> 00:41:45,740
即使他们对答案分歧严重
even though they passionately disagree about the answer.

783
00:41:45,860 --> 00:41:47,780
你失去意识 你就失去了你的灵魂
When you lose consciousness,you lose your soul.

784
00:41:47,890 --> 00:41:49,110
你就失去了一切
You lose everything.

785
00:41:49,230 --> 00:41:51,180
世界已无你的任何东西
The world does not exist anymore for you.

786
00:41:51,290 --> 00:41:53,450
你的友人已不复存在
Your friends don't exist anymore.

787
00:41:53,560 --> 00:41:55,790
你已不复存在 一切都木有了
You don't exist. Everything is lost.

788
00:41:55,900 --> 00:41:58,920
若是你以表面价值来看待这些临死经历的话
If you take these near-death experiences at face value,

789
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:03,990
那么他们认为思想和意识
then they suggest that the mind or the consciousness

790
00:42:04,110 --> 00:42:07,200
貌似无须肉体就能发挥作用的
seems to function without the physical body.

791
00:42:07,310 --> 00:42:09,170
哈梅罗夫医生：我认为量子处理
I think the quantum approach

792
00:42:09,280 --> 00:42:10,870
意识原则上能够
to consciousness can,in principle,

793
00:42:10,980 --> 00:42:14,510
解释我们为何在这里 我们的目的何在
explain why we're here and what our purpose is

794
00:42:14,620 --> 00:42:18,080
以及死后再生和轮回
and also the possibility of life after death and reincarnation

795
00:42:18,190 --> 00:42:20,340
在脱离凡胎后意识长期存在的可能性
and the persistence of consciousness

796
00:42:20,460 --> 00:42:22,080
在脱离凡胎后意识长期存在的可能性
after our bodies give up.

797
00:42:22,190 --> 00:42:27,450
亚历山大博士：我深信不疑
I have great belief and knowledge

798
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:30,550
我们的灵魂美妙地存在于这个尘世之外
that there is a wonderful existence

799
00:42:30,670 --> 00:42:33,820
我们的灵魂美妙地存在于这个尘世之外
for our souls outside of this earthly realm,

800
00:42:33,940 --> 00:42:37,630
那就是我们真实情况
and that is our true reality.

801
00:42:37,740 --> 00:42:41,800
我们离开这个世界的时候都会发现它离开了
And we all find that out when we leave this earth.

802
00:42:41,910 --> 00:42:45,670
最终 我们每个人都将发现真相
Ultimately,every one of us will discover the truth.

803
00:42:45,780 --> 00:42:49,440
不过我们究竟会不会在死到临头时
But will we ever enter our final hour

804
00:42:49,550 --> 00:42:52,980
知晓自己的命运呢？
knowing our fate?

805
00:42:53,090 --> 00:42:56,850
也许有些事情让人类来把握实在是太大了
Perhaps some things really are too big for humans to grasp.

806
00:42:56,960 --> 00:43:01,220
到了那时 我们不得不从我们知道什么
That's when we have to shift from what we know

807
00:43:01,330 --> 00:43:03,510
转变成我们相信什么了
to what we believe.

808
00:43:04,390 --> 00:43:06,390
-- 感谢观赏 --

